{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/766180-living-animals-in-a-beast-s-lair","id":766180,"title":"Living animals in a Beast's Lair?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-15T05:05:36-08:00","id":766180,"title":"Living animals in a Beast's Lair?","content":"So... what happens to animal who are brought into a Beast's lair? Do any other creatures, Astral or not, inhabit a Beast's Lair? If a Beast has a sprawling jungle as a Lair is it devoid of life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T11:22:28-08:00","id":766402,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Lair is a narratively active place, so the short answer is: if that's what your character wants. As we lack much of the information on the Astral Realms, it's hard to definitively rule on how that'd work mechanically, but Kinship would likely be a requirement, particularly when dealing with Astral Entities or other Ephemeral Beings in the Lair. As to material beings (Supernatural or otherwise), some will be harder to bring in then others.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T14:49:15-08:00","id":766554,"title":"","content":"According to word of god during playtest/spoilers, lairs can be inhabited. Or rather seem to be inhabited- a castle can have servants, a prison might have prisoners and guards, an ocean might have sealife, etc, but they aren't real, more like NPCs in a videogame.<br /> <br /> I suppose if you want to have a mechanical benefit from it or gain a benefit from having actual animals or whatever, I'd suggest making it a lair trait or a merit, perhaps naming it menagerie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T18:47:57-08:00","id":766740,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall there is an Infested Tilt...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T19:38:01-08:00","id":766762,"title":"","content":"Something could have been done with the ephemeral rules section...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T00:42:59-08:00","id":766906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/766180-living-animals-in-a-beast-s-lair#post766180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... what happens to animal who are brought into a Beast's lair? Do any other creatures, Astral or not, inhabit a Beast's Lair? If a Beast has a sprawling jungle as a Lair is it devoid of life?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could make an interesting argument that &quot;real&quot; animals brought to the Lair should slowly <i>change</i>, developing odd traits . . . possibly even becoming the Primordial equivalent of cryptids:<ul><li>You know they're there. You hear them scuttling behind you, and through the darkness. From the sounds, there must be tens of thousands of them by now. But no matter how fast you turn your head, or get the lights on, they're always gone. Set something down, though, and look away . . . and you may never see it again. Why, oh why, didn't you kill that cockroach when you had a chance?</li> <li>Its just a parrot. You keep telling yourself that. But after years of living in a Namtaru's undersea cave . . . It spends its time singing disturbing songs about long lost ships, and making cryptic prophecies about the future. And why does it keep looking at you like that?!?</li> <li>The snake eggs are starting to hatch! How cool is that? They actually hatched for you! The little snake sticks its head out of the egg . . .and then a second head . . and a third . . .</li> <li>Maggie was just a mangy old hound you found out on the street. Thin, and stringy, with a matted coat and big chocolate eyes . . . how could you leave her there? After a couple of months, though, she was happy and healthy again. The other day, though, you found her gnawing a bunch of bones . . . bones you didn't give her. Bones that look distinctly human. And is it just you, or have her eyes turned red?</li> </ul>After all, a lot of the old stories have &quot;lesser&quot; monsters woven into the narrative. Things that weren't famous enough, or striking enough (one guy had a flock of man-eating sheep, for example), to get their own myth. They weren't necessarily allied to the main monster . . . but they were there. And it does make a certain degree of sense that exposure to the Dream would slowly turn man's best friend into monster's . . .<br /> <br /> My suggestion would be to keep any such changes thematically appropriate to both the Beast's Lair and Legend. Worms released into a desert chamber might go <i>Tremors (</i>maybe even <i>Dune</i> or <i>Beetlejuice</i>). A cockatrice might hatch from a chicken's egg, if the egg hatches in the Lair of a medieval Beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: And, of course, if they're actually helpful to (or under the control of) the Beast, they need to be paid for, just like any other advantage, merit, or Lair trait","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-16-2015, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T06:57:43-08:00","id":767035,"title":"","content":"Personally I think that Vorlon is right, if it's going to actually give an advantage then it needs to be paid for as a retainer/ally or something. But otherwise, if it's purely cosmetic and thematic, I see no harm in just adding something in for the purposes of story. As the Lair grows, why not strengthen the appearance of it too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5610-aslan751","name":"aslan751","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T13:29:41-08:00","id":767279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/766180-living-animals-in-a-beast-s-lair?p=766906#post766906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could make an interesting argument that &quot;real&quot; animals brought to the Lair should slowly <i>change</i>, developing odd traits . . . possibly even becoming the Primordial equivalent of cryptids:<ul><li>You know they're there. You hear them scuttling behind you, and through the darkness. From the sounds, there must be tens of thousands of them by now. But no matter how fast you turn your head, or get the lights on, they're always gone. Set something down, though, and look away . . . and you may never see it again. Why, oh why, didn't you kill that cockroach when you had a chance?</li> <li>Its just a parrot. You keep telling yourself that. But after years of living in a Namtaru's undersea cave . . . It spends its time singing disturbing songs about long lost ships, and making cryptic prophecies about the future. And why does it keep looking at you like that?!?</li> <li>The snake eggs are starting to hatch! How cool is that? They actually hatched for you! The little snake sticks its head out of the egg . . .and then a second head . . and a third . . .</li> <li>Maggie was just a mangy old hound you found out on the street. Thin, and stringy, with a matted coat and big chocolate eyes . . . how could you leave her there? After a couple of months, though, she was happy and healthy again. The other day, though, you found her gnawing a bunch of bones . . . bones you didn't give her. Bones that look distinctly human. And is it just you, or have her eyes turned red?</li> </ul>After all, a lot of the old stories have &quot;lesser&quot; monsters woven into the narrative. Things that weren't famous enough, or striking enough (one guy had a flock of man-eating sheep, for example), to get their own myth. They weren't necessarily allied to the main monster . . . but they were there. And it does make a certain degree of sense that exposure to the Dream would slowly turn man's best friend into monster's . . .<br /> <br /> My suggestion would be to keep any such changes thematically appropriate to both the Beast's Lair and Legend. Worms released into a desert chamber might go <i>Tremors (</i>maybe even <i>Dune</i> or <i>Beetlejuice</i>). A cockatrice might hatch from a chicken's egg, if the egg hatches in the Lair of a medieval Beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: And, of course, if they're actually helpful to (or under the control of) the Beast, they need to be paid for, just like any other advantage, merit, or Lair trait</div> </div> </div> </div>Our new clich\u00e9 Beast: a highwayman with the soul of a Hydra and an unusually large pet Hermit Crab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T15:48:33-08:00","id":767390,"title":"","content":"Yo dawg, I heard you like Beast, so I put beasts in your Lair so you can beast while you Feast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:52:27-08:00","id":769897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/766180-living-animals-in-a-beast-s-lair?p=767279#post767279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Our new clich\u00e9 Beast: a highwayman with the soul of a Hydra and an unusually large pet Hermit Crab.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. . . I could get behind that - particularly for a short story. A Beast breaks the arms &amp; legs of a hunter (or Hero), and tosses them into a pit Chamber (or on a deserted beach Chamber) to rot. At first, he thinks he's trapped there all alone, with the bones of other unfortunates. Then one of the skulls starts to stir . . .and the hunter realizes a Dream-mutated hermit crab has claimed the skull as it's shell. Other hermit crabs, clearly in need of shells, start crawling out of the dark and the water, and start tapping him with their claws . . .<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><i>Edit:</i></u> I could also see a Dream-twisted crab using the entire corpse as sort of a zombie-shell. Personally, though, I think I'd prefer using roaches or maggots as the basis for such a creature. That way, you get the lurching motion, <i>and</i> it sheds maggots/roaches as it stumbles towards you, trying to talk . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 11-20-2015, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T03:00:48-08:00","id":793037,"title":"","content":"You know, this makes me wonder if other things could be affected like that, inanimate ones. Could an animated statue gain some sentience if it stays in the lair of a beast, or start moving to the beast's tune? Could a vehicle, one already affected in some otherworldly way, gain some autonomy or maybe act to the Beast's whims in some way? Maybe a portrait that spends a little too much time hanging on the lair's walls start looking at its viewers in turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T08:00:37-08:00","id":793092,"title":"","content":"Clip from 1:22 is your answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l9g2w6XPoYs\" data-code=\"l9g2w6XPoYs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/l9g2w6XPoYs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T08:37:41-08:00","id":793108,"title":"","content":"The Staff Merit can represent a menagerie easily enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T13:48:45-08:00","id":793259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/766180-living-animals-in-a-beast-s-lair?p=793108#post793108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Staff Merit can represent a menagerie easily enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>So could the Ally or Retainer merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T11:52:19-08:00","id":793706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/766180-living-animals-in-a-beast-s-lair?p=793259#post793259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So could the Ally or Retainer merits.</div> </div> </div> </div> Allies and Retainers are more directly useable while the staff merit is there to fill in the blanks. (single automatic success on some rolls compared to actually rolling).<br /> <br /> So I'd represent a Pet with the Ally or Retainer merit, background life could be represented by Staff. Best of both worlds! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}